\
## The "Ammunition Factory" Architecture\
\
* The Pre-Prime Stage: P1S is injected into sacrificial casings (or the P1S itself is the casing) on a conveyor or carousel.\
* The Cold-Soak Stage: The shells move through a liquid nitrogen bath or spray, reaching their "critical brittle state" before they ever reach the gun.\
* The Induction Chamber: The "primed" shell enters the EMF field. Since it is already at cryogenic temperatures, the induction heater only needs to perform the final flash-vaporization.\
* The Ejection: The vapor and shrapnel are expelled through the permanent "shoot," and the next pre-cooled shell immediately rotates into place.\
\
